Synthetic production CLI proof for PR #3689
Source head: 926f0f12c
Build: swift build --product CodexBarCLI --jobs 2 (passed, 65.92 s)

Isolation: synthetic HOME, CFFIXED_USER_HOME, TMPDIR, config and PATH;
CODEXBAR_DISABLE_KEYCHAIN_ACCESS=1 and CODEXBAR_SUPPRESS_TEST_KEYCHAIN_ACCESS=1.
macOS sandbox-exec denies network access, other-process metadata, and file access
under the real home except the rebuilt .build (read-only) and this fixture directory.
The sandbox's denial of real-home reads and allowance of fixture reads were checked.
No installed agy, real OAuth account, browser session, or Keychain was used.

Ambient fixture: executable agy in the first PATH directory. It appends every argv
to a marker, returns numeric 1.2.2 for --version, otherwise exits 19 with synthetic
stderr. Invalid overrides are a missing path, empty string, whitespace-only string,
and an existing non-executable file.

Invalid override and positive control command:
  codexbar usage --provider antigravity --source cli --format json --log-level debug --json-output
For every invalid override: exit 1, no sentinel invocation, and the debug sources
field records antigravity.cli-https (cli): skipped: unavailable.
The no-override positive control invokes the same allowed sentinel, including
-p /usage, proving that isolation itself did not suppress ambient executable discovery.

Scoped Auto input: valid sentinel override and ANTIGRAVITY_OAUTH_CREDENTIALS_JSON={};
the synthetic credential envelope is rejected before any HTTP request.
  codexbar diagnose --provider antigravity --format json
  codexbar usage --provider antigravity --source auto --format json --log-level debug --json-output
Both run only --version; neither launches a managed session nor invokes -p /usage.
The export preserves the exclusion category and the usage debug log contains only
safe categories. Neither output contains the synthetic private-response marker.

